
$CATEGORY: GATE CSE Curated/Algorithms

::Curated_ALG_001::[plain]Using the Master Theorem or the recursion-tree method, the tight asymptotic bound for the recurrence T(n) \= 2T(n/2) + n is {~Theta(2^n) ~Theta(n) =Theta(n log n) ~Theta(n^2)}
####Source: Curated - Recurrences

::Curated_ALG_002::[plain]Using the Master Theorem or the recursion-tree method, the tight asymptotic bound for the recurrence T(n) \= T(n/2) + n is {~Theta(n^2) =Theta(n) ~Theta(n log n) ~Theta(2^n)}
####Source: Curated - Recurrences

::Curated_ALG_003::[plain]Using the Master Theorem or the recursion-tree method, the tight asymptotic bound for the recurrence T(n) \= 2T(n/2) + n log n is {=Theta(n log^2 n) ~Theta(n log n) ~Theta(n) ~Theta(n^2)}
####Source: Curated - Recurrences

::Curated_ALG_004::[plain]Using the Master Theorem or the recursion-tree method, the tight asymptotic bound for the recurrence T(n) \= 4T(n/2) + n is {~Theta(n) ~Theta(n log n) ~Theta(2^n) =Theta(n^2)}
####Source: Curated - Recurrences

::Curated_ALG_005::[plain]Using the Master Theorem or the recursion-tree method, the tight asymptotic bound for the recurrence T(n) \= T(n-1) + n is {=Theta(n^2) ~Theta(2^n) ~Theta(n) ~Theta(n log n)}
####Source: Curated - Recurrences

::Curated_ALG_006::[plain]Using the Master Theorem or the recursion-tree method, the tight asymptotic bound for the recurrence T(n) \= 2T(n-1) + 1 is {~Theta(n^2) ~Theta(n log n) ~Theta(n) =Theta(2^n)}
####Source: Curated - Recurrences

