::Curated_ALG_032::[plain]Dijkstra's single-source shortest path algorithm can produce incorrect results with negative edge weights because {~it requires the graph to be complete ~it cannot handle more than V - 1 edges ~it always performs exactly V iterations =a vertex whose distance is finalized may later need to be updated}
####Source: Curated - Graph Algorithms

::Curated_ALG_033::[plain]The Bellman-Ford algorithm detects a negative weight cycle reachable from the source by {~running Dijkstra after one pass ~checking whether the graph is connected ~sorting the edges by weight =performing one extra relaxation round and checking whether any distance still decreases}
####Source: Curated - Graph Algorithms

