::Curated_DB_017::[plain]Relation R(A, B, C, D) has the functional dependencies AB -> C and AB -> D. The highest normal form satisfied by R is {=BCNF ~1NF ~3NF ~2NF}
####Source: Curated - Normalization

::Curated_DB_018::[plain]A BCNF decomposition is always {~dependency preserving but not necessarily lossless ~neither lossless nor dependency preserving =lossless but not necessarily dependency preserving ~both lossless and dependency preserving}
####Source: Curated - Normalization

::Curated_DB_019::[plain]3NF is often preferred over BCNF because a 3NF decomposition {~never requires joins ~always has fewer tables ~eliminates all redundancy =can always be made both lossless and dependency preserving}
####Source: Curated - Normalization

::Curated_DB_020::[plain]A relation is in 2NF if it is in 1NF and {~every determinant is a superkey ~it has no multivalued dependencies =every non-prime attribute is fully functionally dependent on every candidate key ~it has at most one candidate key}
####Source: Curated - Normalization

